  "verification": {
    "status": "unverified",
    "needs_teacher_verification": true,
    "note": "Sourced from the Sri Chaitanya Junior Fastrack zoology section, SAQ chapter 8 'Locomotion & Reproduction' (book p.40, question 38). Zoology holds only ONE source book — the TSBIE Basic Learning Material in hand covers physics only, and no zoology board paper is in the corpus — so the two-book union check and the past-paper back-test are both STRUCTURALLY IMPOSSIBLE for this card, not merely unrun; 'not checked' must never be read as 'checked and clean'. The mark split is this card's claim until a Telangana IPE teacher confirms it. APPEARANCES: the book prints [TS M-16] and [IPE-14]; the bare IPE-14 citation predates the bifurcation and is stored with no board. TEXT BEYOND THE BOOK: the book writes only that 'nucleus, basal granules, chromatophores and cytoplasm undergo division'; the words 'by mitosis' are added here, because nuclear division in Euglena is mitotic (the nuclear membrane persists, so it is called intranuclear mitosis) and a student who writes only 'divides' loses the chance at that mark. FIGURE SCOPE: the book prints five lettered stages A to E; this figure draws four named stages plus labels."
  },
