    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "s1_before",
        "kind": "text",
        "label": "Before the split",
        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "Preparation",
        "lines": [
          "Euglena multiplies by longitudinal binary",
          "fission when conditions are favourable.",
          "The stigma, the paraflagellar body and the",
          "contractile vacuole disappear first.",
          "The nucleus divides into two by mitosis.",
          "The basal granules, the chromatophores and",
          "the cytoplasm also divide."
        ],
        "why": "Three organelles are broken down before the cell splits and the same three are rebuilt afterwards, so listing them here sets up the last step of the answer.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Leaving out the three organelles that disappear. They are named again at the end and carry marks twice.",
          "Writing amitosis. The nucleus of Euglena divides by mitosis."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Three go first and the same three come back last: stigma, paraflagellar body, contractile vacuole.",
        "margin_note": "Favourable conditions, then the three organelles, then the nuclear division."
      },
      {
        "id": "s2_split",
        "kind": "text",
        "label": "The longitudinal split",
        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "Groove",
        "lines": [
          "A longitudinal groove then appears in the",
          "middle of the anterior end.",
          "The groove deepens and extends backwards",
          "towards the posterior end.",
          "It runs along the long axis of the body and",
          "divides the organism into two halves.",
          "The split therefore begins at the front and",
          "finishes at the hind end."
        ],
        "why": "The word longitudinal is a statement about the plane of the cut, so the answer must say that the groove runs along the long axis and travels from the anterior end backwards.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Writing that the groove starts at the posterior end. It starts at the ANTERIOR end.",
          "Describing a cut across the body. That is transverse fission in Paramecium."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Longitudinal means along the length; the groove opens at the front and travels backwards.",
        "margin_note": "Say where the groove starts and which way it travels. Both facts carry the mark."
